{"content":"# Self-contained test helpers for the assignForReview suite

💡 **SUGGESTION — helper duplication / drift risk**

This block duplicates `test_trackers.js`'s helper set (`recorder`, `JIRA_TICKET`, `jiraMocks`, `loadTrackers`) — now the only second copy in `js/unit-tests/`. Self-containment is the right call given the harness has no shared-fixture include (a cross-file, load-order-dependent helper was exactly what broke CI with `ReferenceError`), but note the copies have **already diverged**:

```js
// test_trackers.js (canonical)
var JIRA_TICKET = {
    key: 'PROJ-123',
    ...
    assignee: { displayName: 'Jane Doe', accountId: 'acc-1' },
    labels: ['backend', 'wip'],
    ...
};

// this file
var JIRA_TICKET = {
    key: 'PROJ-1',
    ...
    assignee: null,
    labels: [],
    ...
};
```

`JIRA_TICKET` is an adapted fixture (PROJ-1, `assignee: null` — fitting for the "without an initiator" suite), and `jiraMocks`' comment timestamp differs in format (`2026-09-07T10:00:00Z` vs `2026-09-07T10:00:00.000+0000`). The PR description says "verbatim shapes from test_trackers.js", which is true for `recorder` (byte-identical) but not for the fixture — a one-line "adapted from test_trackers.js; keep in sync on fixture-shape changes" note would prevent a future reader from assuming the two are interchangeable.

Optional follow-up: if the harness ever grows a shared-fixture mechanism, migrate both files onto it. Also note `jiraMocks`' `removeLabelFails` option and `jira_create_ticket_basic` mock are unused by this suite — harmless copy-compat, but dead weight here.
